{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/EnsemblesS3\/documentation\/EnsemblesS3\/S3CloudFileSystem","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A cloud file system backed by Amazon S3, using the AWS SDK for Swift.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembless3\/s3cloudfilesystem"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/EnsemblesS3\/documentation\/EnsemblesS3"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"S3CloudFileSystem"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"class","title":"S3CloudFileSystem","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"S3CloudFileSystem"}],"modules":[{"name":"EnsemblesS3"}],"externalID":"s:11EnsemblesS30B15CloudFileSystemC"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/EnsemblesS3\/9Ensembles15CloudFileSystemP","doc:\/\/EnsemblesS3\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/EnsemblesS3\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"S3CloudFileSystem"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This backend requires the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AWSS3"},{"type":"text","text":" product from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/awslabs\/aws-sdk-swift"},{"type":"text","text":". With the source distribution,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"enable the ","type":"text"},{"code":"S3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" package trait and SPM resolves it automatically. With the binary distribution","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(XCFrameworks), add aws-sdk-swift as a separate package dependency in your project."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"S3 is a flat key-value store, not a hierarchical file system. This backend","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulates directory semantics using key prefixes and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" delimiters — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard S3 convention. For example, the Ensembles path"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ensembleId\/events\/data.json"},{"type":"text","text":" maps to the S3 key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<keyPrefix>ensembleId\/events\/data.json"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Directory creation writes a zero-byte marker object with a trailing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" key."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Directory listing uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ListObjectsV2"},{"text":" with a delimiter to discover","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“subdirectories” via common prefixes. This approach is compatible with S3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"console browsing and third-party tools.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The app configures an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S3Client"},{"text":" with its own credentials and injects it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at init time:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let s3Client = try await S3Client()","let cloudFS = S3CloudFileSystem(","    client: s3Client,","    bucketName: \"my-bucket\",","    keyPrefix: \"ensembles\/\"",")"]},{"anchor":"Authentication","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Authentication"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The AWS SDK for Swift resolves credentials automatically from the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"credential provider chain. Configure credentials using any of:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Environment variables","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and optionally ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AWS_SESSION_TOKEN"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared credentials file"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.aws\/credentials"},{"type":"text","text":" (set via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aws configure"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IAM role"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Automatic on EC2, ECS, and Lambda"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SSO"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Run ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aws sso login"},{"text":", then configure ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.aws\/config"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Default credentials (auto-resolved from environment\/config)","let s3Client = try await S3Client()","","\/\/ Explicit region","let config = try await S3Client.S3ClientConfiguration(region: \"us-west-2\")","let s3Client = S3Client(config: config)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Compatible Services","anchor":"Compatible-Services","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This backend works with any S3-compatible service by configuring a custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"endpoint on the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S3Client"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MinIO"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — self-hosted object storage","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloudflare R2"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — zero egress fees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backblaze B2"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — low-cost cloud storage","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DigitalOcean Spaces"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — simple object storage","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let config = try await S3Client.S3ClientConfiguration(","    region: \"auto\",","    endpoint: \"https:\/\/your-minio-host:9000\"",")","let s3Client = S3Client(config: config)","let cloudFS = S3CloudFileSystem(","    client: s3Client,","    bucketName: \"my-bucket\",","    keyPrefix: \"ensembles\/\"",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Threading","anchor":"Threading","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This class is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unchecked Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S3Client"},{"type":"text","text":" handles its own thread"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safety internally. Mutable state ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loggedIn"},{"type":"text","text":") is only written during"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connect()"},{"type":"text","text":" and error handling."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"gene